{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2006-12-14","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2017-09-30","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/department/narrative":[{"1":"MCO-EGY","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/email":[{"1":"v.jijyan@ifad.org"}],"/job-title/narrative":[{"1":"Head MCO/Country Director","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Jijyan, Vrej","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"The overall project objective is to contribute to poverty reduction and improved livelihoods of the target population in the project area. The intermediate objectives will be to empower the target group to create sustained employment and increase income through (i) SME development and microfinance; (ii) farming system research and extension to help small farmers achieve higher returns per unit of land and water; and (iii) improved water management for the more rational use and equitable distribution of available water for sustained irrigation. An important objective of the project is to help establish a sustainable microfinancesystem by extending microfinance support from the Social Fund for Development (SFD) into the rural areas of Upper Egypt and forming partnerships with commercial banks. It is also anticipated that project support for the establishment, empowerment and training of WUAs at the branch (secondary) canal level, and theirparticipation in water boards at the district level, will contribute to the establishment of a sustainable and fully participatory system for water management.","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A12"}],"/description/narrative":[{"1":"More informatio